-The module also holds the on-device engine, OnDeviceSttEngine, which implements the core SttEngine port: it asks the loader for the model on every call, and the loader checks the stamp of the unpacked files before the engine opens them; it decodes one request at a time, and reports every problem as a failure result instead of throwing. The native adapter that creates the recognizer exists (`SherpaOnnxRecognizerFactory`). The module cannot transcribe until the app supplies the sherpa-onnx release file and passes the factory to the model loader; that wiring is the app's, not this module's. `SherpaOnnxWordStreamFactory` is the public factory for the word stream: `create()` returns a `FedWordStream`, a core word stream that also takes audio through `feed`; it reports the number of chunks and samples dropped since the last start() because the queue was full, exposed as the read-only members `droppedChunks` and `droppedSamples`. The app is to build its stream through that factory. At install the module records a stamp of the four unpacked files, and the word stream factory refuses a model whose stamp is missing or does not match them. How it behaves on a device has not been tested.
+The module also holds the on-device engine, OnDeviceSttEngine, which implements the core SttEngine port: it asks the loader for the model on every call, and the loader checks the stamp of the unpacked files before the engine opens them; it decodes one request at a time, and reports every problem as a failure result instead of throwing. The native adapter that creates the recognizer exists (`SherpaOnnxRecognizerFactory`). The module cannot transcribe until the app supplies the sherpa-onnx release file and passes the factory to the model loader; that wiring is the app's, not this module's. `SherpaOnnxWordStreamFactory` is the public factory for the word stream: `create()` returns a `FedWordStream`, a core word stream that also takes audio through `feed`. The app is to build its stream through that factory. At install the module records a stamp of the four unpacked files, and the word stream factory refuses a model whose stamp is missing or does not match them. How it behaves on a device has not been tested.
